_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977622/assets/3f3f1422eca9190a5e0827da456315ba88b074f0bf5e9aab1bb325d131bf1984.png)\n\nAnother solution $X$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={330}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we subtract ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={330}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-30\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=30\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977622/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec26c54c8f04ebce6ed3bc4053aaf832400adca120bb72ae9828c01eaaaa7850"} {"question" "q-274900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ec93222686d7127d6a0b0f230de357b7dd6a9281db371524cde917072b9cb1b"} {"question" "q-274900" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977622/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec26c54c8f04ebce6ed3bc4053aaf832400adca120bb72ae9828c01eaaaa7850"} {"question" "q-274900" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977622/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec26c54c8f04ebce6ed3bc4053aaf832400adca120bb72ae9828c01eaaaa7850"} {"question" "q-274900" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acade